==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|NL.|-}}, from {{der|en|grc|χαλκός||copper}}. Despite the appearance in English of a possible relation of ''chalco-'' to ''[[chalk#Etymology|chalk]]'', and any plausible semantic and cognate connections between limestones and ores in ancient times, the terms are not related by any known cognation<!--whether there was ever any cognation between {{m|grc|χαλκός}} and {{m|grc|χάλιξ}} remains untraceable to date-->. Note also the hard ''ch'' sound (/k/) in ''chalco-'' and words generated therefrom, which differs from the soft ''ch'' sound in {{m|en|chalk}}<!--The pronunciation difference is artifactual rather than etymological, but it is nonetheless pedagogically useful as a memory aid for the [[false cognate]] status-->.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|en|/ˈkælkoʊ/}}

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# {{l|en|copper#Noun|Copper}}; relatedly, also {{l|en|bronze#Noun}} or {{l|en|brass#Noun}}.
